The '''2026 St Helens Metropolitan Borough Council election''' was held on 7 May 2026, alongside the [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]] being held on the same day.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Elections and voting - St Helens Borough Council |url=https://sthelens.gov.uk/elections |archive-url=http://web.archive.org/web/20251107160246/https://sthelens.gov.uk/elections |archive-date=2025-11-07 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=St Helens Borough Council |language=en}}</ref> All 48 members of [[St Helens Metropolitan Borough Council]] will be elected.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-05-02 |title=Details of elections taking place - and why there isn't any for St Helens Council |url=https://www.sthelensstar.co.uk/news/24292769.details-elections-taking-place-st-helens-today/ |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=St Helens Star |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In [[2022 St Helens Metropolitan Borough Council election|2022]], Labour retained control of the council.<ref>{{Cite news |title=St Helens result - Local Elections 2022 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2022/england/councils/E08000013 |access-date=2026-01-27 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

